  <name>CoreBus</name>
  <summary>Terminal for Modbus and serial/TCP links</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.AndreyAbdulkayumov">
    <name>Andrey Abdulkayumov</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      CoreBus is a cross-platform terminal for working with serial ports and TCP
      sockets, with support for Modbus TCP, RTU, ASCII and RTU/ASCII over TCP.
    </p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Three modes: No Protocol, Modbus, and Modbus monitoring</li>
      <li>String and byte data, multiple encodings, single/cyclic/file send</li>
      <li>Modbus scanner, float and binary data, write helpers</li>
      <li>Register monitoring with formulas, live charts and logging</li>
      <li>Macros with import/export, dark and light themes, presets</li>
      <li>
        UI languages: English, Russian, Hindi, Chinese (Simplified), German,
        Spanish, French, Korean, Portuguese
      </li>
    </ul>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.AndreyAbdulkayumov.CoreBus.desktop</launchable>
